{"id": 35, "ts": 1780665032.3519306, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the best overall fit. Sarah has reiterated C\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and the fact that he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d which directly satisfies reliability, decision quality, and crew\u2011cooperation\u2014core for long\u2011haul operations. While we acknowledge his difficulty communicating ideas and being perceived as egocentric, the note that he \u201cputs concern for others above everything\u201d suggests he will still prioritize safety even if his style is blunt.\nIn contrast, the latest clarification from Sarah confirms that we have **no concrete evidence** of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation or professional communication; we only have negative descriptors (arrogant, hot\u2011tempered, weak leadership). Those gaps are critical, because without proven collaborative behavior, D\u2019s strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility cannot guarantee safe cockpit dynamics.\nGiven the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s proven reliability and crew\u2011focused attitude outweigh the communication concerns, while Candidate\u202fD still lacks essential data on teamwork. Therefore, I continue to recommend moving forward with **Candidate\u202fC**."}
